{
  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Databricks audit log (system.access.audit / workspace audit log) → AKSI control ID mapping. Databricks is the dominant unified analytics + ML platform; agents on Databricks query Lakehouse data, train models, deploy notebooks, run jobs, attach to GPU clusters, register models in Unity Catalog, transition versions in MLflow, and increasingly call Vector Search and Genie (GenAI) workloads. The audit-log surface is rich: service_name partitions the universe (workspace, jobs, clusters, sql, unityCatalog, mlflow, notebook, genie, dlt, vectorSearch, feature), action_name names the verb, response.status_code carries authorization outcome, and the is_compute_attached / compute_kind / is_genai_use_case fields tag the GenAI workload context. Mapping is service_name + action_name driven with overlays for GPU instance creation (PR-04 cost / blast radius), Unity Catalog destructive operations (PR-02 FAIL), MLflow auto-promotion to Production with no approver (PR-02 FAIL — same as the dedicated MLflow importer), and notebook shell-out detection (PR-03 FAIL — SQL→OS gadget on Databricks). Cross-workspace and high-volume cluster-creation patterns produce synthetic findings. The importer NEVER stores query text, notebook content, raw request_params values (key list only — params can carry secrets like access tokens), full email (DOMAIN ONLY), full IP (mask /16), full user_agent (first 80 + sha256), or raw error messages.",
  "_metadata": {
    "source_format": "databricks",
    "schema": "databricks-system-audit-v1",
    "owner": "ancilis-importers",
    "cross_workspace_threshold": 3,
    "cluster_creation_burst": 10,
    "cluster_creation_window_seconds": 3600,
    "user_agent_prefix_length": 80,
    "gpu_node_patterns": [
      "Standard_NV*",
      "Standard_NC*",
      "Standard_ND*",
      "g4dn.*",
      "g5.*",
      "p2.*",
      "p3.*",
      "p4d.*",
      "p4de.*",
      "p5.*"
    ],
    "admin_action_patterns": [
